<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd"[]><!-- Original file name: 6872A6E9-237F-42E3-8C5D-A7005F8CEBAF.dita --><topic id="GUID-24962C97-1DB5-4F14-9F68-54BA400D4D9F" xml:lang="en-US"><title>SODIMM 2DPC Daisy (B2B)</title><body><section id="SECTION_6872A6E9-237F-42E3-8C5D-A7005F8CEBAF"><p>Pcb Type &amp; Thickness: Type-3, 0.9mm</p><fig id="FIG_SODIMM_2DPC_DAISY_B2B_TOPOLOGY_DIAGRAM_1"><title>SODIMM_2DPC_DAISY_B2B_Topology_Diagram</title><image href="../images/GUID-4DA37286-2CEF-4EF3-B309-5D2111F960F2.png" scalefit="yes" id="IMG_SODIMM_2DPC_DAISY_B2B_TOPOLOGY_DIAGRAM_1_PNG" /></fig><fig id="FIG_SODIMM_2DPC_DAISY_BACK_TO_BACK_CONFIGURATION_1"><title>SODIMM_2DPC_DAISY_BACK_TO_BACK_CONFIGURATION</title><image href="../images/GUID-BC9846C1-BF9E-45C9-BC6F-1138C695BA4E.png" scalefit="yes" id="IMG_SODIMM_2DPC_DAISY_BACK_TO_BACK_CONFIGURATION_1_PNG" /></fig><fig id="FIG_DDR5_SODIMM_TOP-PIN_BOTTOM-PIN_LENGTH_PROPAGATION_DEFINITION_1"><title>DDR5 SODIMM Top-Pin Bottom-Pin Length Propagation Definition</title><image href="../images/GUID-BDD47511-85D3-4601-9880-F2072135801B.png" scalefit="yes" id="IMG_DDR5_SODIMM_TOP-PIN_BOTTOM-PIN_LENGTH_PROPAGATION_DEFINITION_1_PNG" /></fig><fig id="FIG_SODIMM_2DPC_DAISY_B2B_TOPOLOGY_CONNECTIVITY_RECOMMENDATION_1"><title>SODIMM_2DPC_DAISY_B2B_Topology_Connectivity_Recommendation</title><image href="../images/GUID-61628FEF-65FD-49B0-A6FC-DBE6C0768A32.png" scalefit="yes" id="IMG_SODIMM_2DPC_DAISY_B2B_TOPOLOGY_CONNECTIVITY_RECOMMENDATION_1_PNG" /></fig><table id="TABLE_6872A6E9-237F-42E3-8C5D-A7005F8CEBAF_1"><title>SODIMM 2DPC Daisy (B2B) Notes</title><tgroup cols="2"><thead><row><entry>Note</entry><entry>Detail</entry></row></thead><tbody><row><entry><p>PCB stackup</p></entry><entry><p>MB Type-3 stackup with minimum 10-layers.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>GND via placement</p></entry><entry><p>For Ch 0/1 Processor breakout, each DQ/ DQS signal via should have a GND via placed orthogonally next to it (within 800 um).  DQ/ DQS signal vias from different bytes should be isolated from each other with a GND via.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>GND via placement</p></entry><entry><p>For Ch 2/3 Processor breakout, each DQ/ DQS signal via should have a GND via placed orthogonally next to it (within 800 um).  DQ/ DQS signal vias from different bytes should be isolated from each other with a GND via.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Reference plane</p></entry><entry><p>Continuous Ground only.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Serpentine routing</p></entry><entry><p>Use 3x of dielectric height for serpentine routing spacing.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Unused signals</p></entry><entry><p>Unused Data Mask pins on DIMMs should be tied to VSS supply. Only a minimal trace width is required to make ensure signal is terminated.  A dedicated GND via is NOT recommended for the data mask pins.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Unused signals</p></entry><entry><p>Unused ECC/ CB and EVENT signals maybe left unconnected at the SODIMM connectors.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Routing</p></entry><entry><p>"Group to Group" spacing in table above is referring to either DQ/ DQS to CLK/ CS/ CA within the same channel, or signals between different channels. DQ S2 and DQS S2 spacing refers DQ 2 DQS spacing.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Routing</p></entry><entry><p>Keep GND stitching via within 250 um from signal transition which changes reference planes.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Routing</p></entry><entry><p>For both Channel 0/1 and 2/3, DQ and DQS signal vias for Segment E should be separated from each other with a GND via between.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Routing</p></entry><entry><p>It is STRONGLY recommended customers follow the RVP board for DDR Processor BO region and via pattern at both Processor and DIMMs</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Routing (voiding)</p></entry><entry><p>Voiding of L2 under SODIMM connector DQ and DQS pins is NOT required for any channel in this topology.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Bit/Byte swapping rule</p></entry><entry><p>Bit swapping is allowed within each Byte for all memory technologies. </p><p>DDR5: Byte Swapping is allowed within each x32 channel.</p><p /></entry></row><row><entry><p>Tuning</p></entry><entry><p>Channel 0 and 1 are separate channels routing to the same DIMM. There is no explicit tuning relationship between these 2 channels. This also applies to Channel 2 and 3.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>RESET</p></entry><entry><p>Keep R1 empty; R2 = 0 Ohm; C1 = 0.1 uF (no stuff).</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>EMI/RFI mitigation</p></entry><entry><p>We recommend that in SODIMM 2DPC DAISY B2B designs, the DIMMS that are on the Far side of the SOC to get populated first for 0R2R configuration.</p><p>For CH0 and CH1 the 8H connector should be populated first and 4H connector (near SOC can be left open)</p><p>For CH2 and CH3 the 4H connector (Far from SOC) should be populated first and 8H connector can be left open</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Length compensation between top and bottom pins</p></entry><entry><p>For any signal connected to a SODIMM right angle connector TOP side pin, increase the "effective" motherboard length of that signal by 3mm (~20ps) for the purposes of length matching rules.  "Effective" length (for length matching) = motherboard length + 3mm.  Designers should not just generically add 3mm of length directly to the physical motherboard signals connected to the TOP pin of a right angle SODIMM connector.</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Include SODIMM connector top pin vs bottom pin compensation in length matching</p></entry><entry><p>Required</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>Number of vias allowed</p></entry><entry><p>DQ/ RDQS/WCK CA/ CS/ CLK: Max 2 vias. </p><p>ALERT Signal: Max 3 Via</p><p>RESET signal may have max 5 via.</p><p /></entry></row></tbody></tgroup></table><table id="TABLE_6872A6E9-237F-42E3-8C5D-A7005F8CEBAF_2"><title>Max number of vias</title><tgroup cols="2"><thead><row><entry>Signal Group</entry><entry>Max Number of Vias Allowed</entry></row></thead><tbody><row><entry><p>CA, CLK, CS, DQ, DQS</p></entry><entry><p>2</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>RCOMP</p></entry><entry><p>1</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>ALERT</p></entry><entry><p>3</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>RESET</p></entry><entry><p>5</p></entry></row></tbody></tgroup></table></section><section id="SECTION_SYSTEM_MEMORY_0D2567A7-00B5-48F8-BA9C-4B330204A25B_6872A6E9-237F-42E3-8C5D-A7005F8CEBAF_LENGTH_MATCHING"><title>Length Matching</title><table id="TABLE_SYSTEM_MEMORY_0D2567A7-00B5-48F8-BA9C-4B330204A25B_6872A6E9-237F-42E3-8C5D-A7005F8CEBAF_LENGTH_MATCHING_1" scale="60"><title>SODIMM 2DPC Daisy (B2B) Length Matching</title><tgroup cols="9"><thead><row valign="top"><entry outputclass="rotate90">Signal Group</entry><entry outputclass="rotate90">Plus/Minus</entry><entry outputclass="rotate90">Reference Group</entry><entry outputclass="rotate90">Within/Group</entry><entry outputclass="rotate90">Up to memory/connector</entry><entry outputclass="rotate90">Length/Delay</entry><entry outputclass="rotate90">Min/Max/Range</entry><entry outputclass="rotate90">Min</entry><entry outputclass="rotate90">Max</entry></row></thead><tbody><row><entry><p>CLK</p></entry><entry><p>-</p></entry><entry><p>DQS</p></entry><entry><p>Channel (x32)</p></entry><entry><p>Same Connector</p></entry><entry><p>Length (mm)</p></entry><entry><p>Range</p></entry><entry><p>-38</p></entry><entry><p>63.5</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>DQ</p></entry><entry><p>-</p></entry><entry><p>DQS</p></entry><entry><p>Byte (x8)</p></entry><entry><p>Same Connector</p></entry><entry><p>Length (mm)</p></entry><entry><p>Range</p></entry><entry><p>-0.5</p></entry><entry><p>0.5</p></entry></row><row><entry><p>DQS_P</p></entry><entry><p>-</p></entry><entry><p>DQS_N</p></entry><entry><p>Pair (P-N)</p></entry><entry><p>Same Connector</p></entry><entry><p>Length (mm)</p></entry><entry><p>Max</p>